<h1>Kristian Armendariz</h1>
<p>22nd Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Announced at the end of July 2026 that he will run again for the seat. No 2027 platform found. In his 2023 run he named public safety, education, and environmental justice as the ward&#39;s biggest issues and proposed mental health clinics, more funding for trade programs, financial literacy workshops, and resources for people experiencing homelessness.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Little Village youth organizer, most recently with the Little Village Community Council as of 2023; finished behind Ald. Michael Rodriguez in the 2023 election.</p>
